WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:05.860
Believe it or not, earning a zero percent
rating on Rotten Tomatoes is quite an achievement.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.259
Reviewing a film is subjective, of course,
so critics pretty much always have opposing

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.060
arguments on the quality of a movie.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.920
But once in a while, a movie comes along that
brings even the most stubborn critics together

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.420
to unanimously agree the film is not worth
your time.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.040
Here are some of the unlucky films that managed
to pull off a zero percent rating.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.240
Jaws: The Revenge

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:33.160
Even if you haven't seen the fourth Jaws movie,
you may have read or heard Michael Caine's

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.220
famous quote on his involvement with the ill-fated
picture.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.460
According to The Telegraph, he admitted,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.600
"I have never seen it, but by all accounts
it was terrible.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.820
However, I have seen the house that it built,
and it is terrific."

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:51.460
1987's Jaws: The Revenge single-handedly ended
the killer shark franchise by being incompetent

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.540
on every level.

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.579
Developed from conception to completion in
less than a year, the movie was rushed and

00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:02.350
careless, with director Joseph Sargent telling
Starlog magazine at the time,

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.880
"This is probably the quickest gestation of
any project, I think, in film history."

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:10.220
"How did we get involved in something that
idiotic?"

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:16.440
The lack of filmmaking expertise on display,
along with an utterly nonsensical premise,

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:22.300
makes for a viewing experience that unfortunately
isn't worth your time, and the critics all

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:22.800
agreed.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:24.240
Gotti

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:30.980
Within days of its limited theatrical release
in 2018, this John Travolta-starring John

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:36.530
Gotti biopic was being confidently hailed
as "the worst mob movie of all time."

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:41.210
It's hard to be 100 percent certain if that's
true, but it's also hard to see how things

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:42.400
could get much worse.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.920
Gotti's greatest sin is that it's incredibly
boring.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:50.720
Bizarrely edited and difficult to follow,
the movie is essentially a long collection

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:55.270
of technically uninteresting scenes, stitched
together into something that only sometimes

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:56.220
looks like a film.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.520
It's confusing how they even got a movie star
in the lead role.

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:04.960
In an effort to combat its 0 percent rating,
producers of the film rolled out an ad campaign

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.220
claiming that it's not a movie for critics,
but rather something general audiences would

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:09.820
enjoy.

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.480
"I don't think so."

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:13.360
Dark Crimes

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:19.090
Jim Carrey became widely-known in the '80s
and '90s for his committed slapstick comedy

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:19.820
performances.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.710
But he later surprised viewers with impressive
turns playing against type in more serious

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:28.820
films like Man on the Moon and Eternal Sunshine
of the Spotless Mind.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:34.960
With all that dramatic talent, it's unfortunate
that 2018's Dark Crimes was such a fail.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:40.260
Focusing on a detective who discovers startling
similarities between a cold case murder and

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:45.150
the plot of a recent novel, Dark Crimes has
an interesting enough concept to root for

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:48.920
the movie from the start, but it never, ever
meets you there.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:54.800
Uncomfortable and unengaging, Dark Crimes
earns its 0 percent rating not through apathy

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:55.680
or blandness.

00:02:55.930 --> 00:03:01.020
Instead, it actively repulses, digging its
way down to the bottom of the barrel, one

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.240
scene of intense violence at a time.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:05.320
Look Who's Talking Now

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:11.810
Capping off the Look Who's Talking trilogy,
1993's Look Who's Talking Now takes the first

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:16.581
two movies' conceit of tough-talking babies
and broadens it with the introduction of a

00:03:16.581 --> 00:03:18.659
team of talking dogs.

00:03:18.659 --> 00:03:24.580
The insane execution is the main problem here,
with a seemingly-family-friendly concept perverted

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:29.599
by enough bad language, innuendo, and adult
humor to shut out the age group that you'd

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.700
think would be the movie's entire audience.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.040
"Whaddya say you and me go play bury the bone?"

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:40.800
As a sequel, Look Who's Talking Now is one
of the all-time-classic examples of the concept

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.280
of diminishing returns.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:47.620
The unexpected franchise had already given
audiences a retread with Look Who's Talking,

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:52.740
Too, making the completely unnecessary third
outing feel all the more puzzling.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:54.540
The Ridiculous 6

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.760
Adam Sandler's early successes have helped
to sustain an entire career's worth of unholy

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:01.600
crapola.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:08.760
But 2015's The Ridiculous 6 is his rock-bottom,
one of the few films that truly deserves distinction

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.860
among the worst movies of all time.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:16.640
In Sandler's early movies, the lowbrow quality
of his humor was still stupid, but it felt

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:17.980
like you were in on a joke.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.660
With The Ridiculous 6, it feels like you are
the joke.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:26.940
It's like the actor took a dare to make the
most offensive, least-capable movie that people

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.080
would still watch.

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:33.660
The film also comes across as mean-spirited,
steeped so heavily in harmful Native American

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:37.880
stereotypes that several actors reportedly
left the set in protest

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:39.980
Max Steel

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:45.520
Superhero movies have spent the last decade
cleaning up at the box office, but that doesn't

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.280
mean the genre is a safe bet.

00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:53.520
Based on a toy line from Mattel, 2016's Max
Steel is a false-start of an effort to bring

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.980
a new franchise to life.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:05:01.060
It focuses on a young man named Max and a
robotic life-form from outer space named Steel,

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:06.490
the latter of which is a joke-cracking snark
machine capable of enveloping itself entirely

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:08.200
around Max like a suit of armor.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:13.210
The result is a movie that tries to combine
the best elements of Iron Man and Transformers,

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:17.400
failing to accomplish either by ultimately
being too bland.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:23.100
Everything in the movie is something you've
seen before, and unfortunately, all this unforgivably

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:27.190
boring film does is remind you of other films
that did it all better.

